.TH NEPLANG 1 "October 2026" "NepLang" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
neplang \- run a NepLang program
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B neplang
.I file.np
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B neplang
runs a program written in NepLang, a small programming language whose keywords are
romanized Nepali words mixed with English technical terms.
Source files must end in
.BR .np .
.PP
Each statement goes on its own line, and
.B #
starts a comment.
.SH LANGUAGE
.TP
.B vana(expr)
Print a value.
.TP
.B name = expr
Create or update a variable.
.TP
.B yedi cond { } natara yedi cond { } natara { }
If / else-if / else.
.B natara
must be on the same line as the closing
.BR } .
.TP
.B jabasamma cond { }
While loop.
.TP
.B ko_lagi i in a..b { }
Count
.I i
from
.I a
up to, but not including,
.IR b .
.TP
.B kaam name(a, b) { farkau expr }
Define a function;
.B farkau
returns a value.
.PP
Values are integers. Comparisons
.B "== != < <= > >="
give 1 or 0, and any non-zero value is true.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
kaam factorial(n) {
    yedi n <= 1 {
        farkau 1
    }
    farkau n * factorial(n \- 1)
}
vana(factorial(6))
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 on a syntax or runtime error, which is printed with its file, line and
column.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/charitraa/Nepa
